# Verbal Ability: reading comprehension and paragraph organization. Passages are original. Key first.
ITEMS = [
    # ---------- Practice Test 1 (Professional) ----------
    S(1, 2, "Main idea", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nMany towns once sent all their garbage to open dumpsites. The dumps smelled, drew rats and leaked dirty water into nearby streams. Today a growing number of barangays sort waste at the source. Kitchen scraps go to compost pits, bottles and cans are sold to junk shops, and only what cannot be used again goes to a sanitary landfill. As a result, trucks make fewer trips and the landfill fills more slowly.\n\nWhat is the passage mainly about?",
      ["How sorting waste reduces what reaches landfills", "Why rats are attracted to open dumpsites", "How junk shops set prices for bottles", "Why towns should build more landfills"],
      "Every sentence after the first leads to one point: sorting at the source means less waste reaches the landfill. Rats and junk shops are details, and the passage never argues for more landfills."),
    S(1, 2, "Inference", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nThe municipal library extended its hours to 8:00 p.m. on weekdays last June. In the months that followed, the number of borrowers rose sharply, and most of the new borrowers signed in after 5:00 p.m. Many of them listed their occupation as office worker or student.\n\nWhat can be inferred from the passage?",
      ["Many borrowers could not visit during office hours", "The library will soon close on weekends", "Students prefer reading at home at night", "The library hired new staff in June"],
      "New borrowers came mostly after 5:00 p.m. and were workers or students, which suggests the old hours did not suit them. Nothing is said about weekends or hiring."),
    S(1, 3, "Author's purpose", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nBefore you sign a contract, read every page, not just the first and the last. Ask about any term you do not understand, and never sign a page with blank spaces that someone else could fill in later. Keep a copy of everything you sign.\n\nWhat is the author's main purpose?",
      ["To advise readers on signing contracts safely", "To explain how contracts are written by lawyers", "To warn readers never to sign any contract", "To describe the history of written contracts"],
      "The passage gives step-by-step advice for signing safely. It does not forbid signing, and it says nothing about how lawyers draft contracts or their history."),
    S(1, 2, "Detail", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nThe province's coffee farmers once sold their beans fresh, at low prices, to traders who visited after harvest. Three years ago a cooperative bought a shared drying and roasting machine. Members now sell roasted coffee in sealed bags to cafes in the city, and their income per kilo has more than doubled.\n\nAccording to the passage, what allowed the farmers to sell to city cafes?",
      ["A shared drying and roasting machine", "A new road built to the city", "Higher prices paid by traders", "A larger coffee harvest each year"],
      "The passage links the change to the cooperative's shared machine, which let members sell roasted, bagged coffee. Roads and harvest size are not mentioned."),
    S(1, 3, "Tone", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nThe new online appointment system was supposed to end the long lines. Instead, the website crashes every morning at eight, the confirmation emails arrive a day late, and applicants still line up outside the gate before dawn. One more improvement like this, and the office may need a second gate.\n\nWhat is the writer's tone?",
      ["Sarcastic", "Admiring", "Neutral", "Hopeful"],
      "The last sentence calls the failure an \"improvement\" and jokes about needing a second gate, which is sarcasm. The listed problems rule out an admiring or hopeful tone."),
    S(1, 3, "Paragraph organization", "Arrange the sentences to form a logical paragraph.\n\n1. Finally, the approved request is forwarded to the cashier for payment.\n2. First, the employee fills out a reimbursement form.\n3. The supervisor then checks the receipts and signs the form.\n4. Next, the employee attaches the official receipts to it.",
      ["2, 4, 3, 1", "2, 3, 4, 1", "4, 2, 3, 1", "2, 4, 1, 3"],
      "The signal words give the order: \"First\" (2), \"Next\" (4), \"then\" (3) and \"Finally\" (1). The supervisor must check the receipts after they are attached."),
    S(1, 2, "Paragraph organization", "Arrange the sentences to form a logical paragraph.\n\n1. These warm waters give storms the energy they need to grow.\n2. The Philippines lies beside the Pacific Ocean, where the sea is warm for much of the year.\n3. This is why the country is hit by many typhoons every year.\n4. Storms that form over the Pacific often move west toward the islands.",
      ["2, 1, 4, 3", "2, 4, 1, 3", "1, 2, 4, 3", "4, 2, 1, 3"],
      "Sentence 2 introduces the setting, 1 explains what \"these warm waters\" do, 4 says where the storms go, and 3 draws the conclusion with \"This is why\"."),
    S(1, 3, "Paragraph organization", "Which sentence best completes the paragraph?\n\n\"Regular exercise helps the body in many ways. It strengthens the heart and lungs and helps control weight. ___\"",
      ["It can also lift mood and improve sleep.", "However, many people have no time to cook.", "Some gyms charge a monthly membership.", "The first marathon was run in Greece."],
      "The paragraph lists benefits of exercise, so the best closing sentence adds more benefits. The others change the topic."),
    S(1, 2, "Vocabulary in context", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nThe town council debated the proposal for three hours. Several members worried about the cost, and one asked for a study of the traffic it would cause. In the end the council decided to __defer__ the vote until the study was complete.\n\nAs used in the passage, \"defer\" most nearly means:",
      ["put off", "cancel", "speed up", "count"],
      "The council waits \"until the study was complete\", so the vote is put off, not cancelled."),
    S(1, 3, "Conclusion", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nA study of public offices found that those using a numbered queue ticket served clients in an average of 12 minutes. Offices without a ticket system averaged 31 minutes, and staff there reported more arguments over who was next in line.\n\nWhich conclusion is best supported by the passage?",
      ["Queue tickets are linked to faster, calmer service", "Queue tickets make staff work longer hours", "Offices without tickets have fewer clients", "Clients prefer offices that open early"],
      "Ticket offices were faster and had fewer arguments, so the passage supports a link between tickets and faster, calmer service. Nothing is said about hours, client numbers or opening times."),

    # ---------- Practice Test 2 (Subprofessional) ----------
    S(2, 1, "Main idea", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nMangroves grow along muddy coasts where rivers meet the sea. Their tangled roots slow down waves and hold the soil in place. Young fish and crabs hide among the roots until they are big enough to swim out to sea. For coastal villages, mangroves are both a shield and a nursery.\n\nWhat is the main idea of the passage?",
      ["Mangroves protect coasts and shelter young sea life", "Mangroves grow best in deep, clear water", "Fishermen should catch fish among the roots", "Crabs are the most common animal at sea"],
      "The last sentence sums it up: mangroves are a shield (against waves) and a nursery (for young fish and crabs). The passage says they grow on muddy coasts, not in deep water."),
    S(2, 1, "Detail", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nThe health center is open from Monday to Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Free vaccinations for children are given every Wednesday morning. Parents must bring the child's vaccination card. Senior citizens may get a free blood pressure check on any weekday.\n\nWhen are free vaccinations for children given?",
      ["Wednesday mornings", "Any weekday", "Monday to Friday afternoons", "Saturday mornings"],
      "The passage says vaccinations are given \"every Wednesday morning\". \"Any weekday\" applies to the blood pressure checks."),
    S(2, 2, "Detail", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nTo renew a business permit, the owner submits the old permit, the barangay clearance and proof of payment of local taxes. The papers are checked at Window 3. If they are complete, the new permit is released at Window 5 after two working days.\n\nWhere are the renewal papers checked?",
      ["At Window 3", "At Window 5", "At the barangay hall", "At the tax office"],
      "Papers are checked at Window 3; Window 5 is where the new permit is released."),
    S(2, 2, "Inference", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nWhen Lorna arrived at the office, the lights were off and the door was locked. A sign on the glass said the building had no power until noon. She sighed, checked her watch and walked to the coffee shop across the street.\n\nWhat can be inferred about Lorna?",
      ["She planned to wait until the office reopened", "She decided to quit her job that morning", "She forgot that it was a holiday", "She had the key to open the door"],
      "She checked the time and went across the street instead of going home, which suggests she meant to wait. The sign explains the closure, so it was not a holiday she forgot."),
    S(2, 2, "Sequence", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nWhen the fire alarm sounds, stop work at once. Leave your belongings and walk, do not run, to the nearest exit. Use the stairs, not the elevator. Once outside, go to the assembly area in the parking lot and wait for the head count.\n\nWhat should employees do right after leaving the building?",
      ["Go to the assembly area", "Return for their belongings", "Take the elevator down", "Call the fire station"],
      "The passage says that once outside, employees go to the assembly area in the parking lot and wait for the head count."),
    S(2, 2, "Paragraph organization", "Arrange the sentences to form a logical paragraph.\n\n1. Then she poured the batter into a greased pan.\n2. First, Rosa mixed the flour, sugar and eggs in a bowl.\n3. After forty minutes, the cake was ready.\n4. She baked it in a hot oven.",
      ["2, 1, 4, 3", "2, 4, 1, 3", "1, 2, 4, 3", "2, 1, 3, 4"],
      "Mixing comes first (2), then pouring into the pan (1), then baking (4), and the cake is ready after forty minutes (3)."),
    S(2, 3, "Paragraph organization", "Arrange the sentences to form a logical paragraph.\n\n1. As a result, many residents now ride the bus to work.\n2. Last year the city opened a new bus route along the main avenue.\n3. Traffic on the avenue has also become lighter.\n4. The buses run every ten minutes and the fare is low.",
      ["2, 4, 1, 3", "2, 1, 4, 3", "4, 2, 1, 3", "2, 4, 3, 1"],
      "Sentence 2 introduces the route, 4 describes it, 1 gives the result (\"As a result\"), and 3 adds a further effect (\"also\")."),
    S(2, 2, "Paragraph organization", "Which sentence best completes the paragraph?\n\n\"Water is precious during the dry season. Fix leaking faucets right away. ___ Use a pail instead of a hose when washing the car.\"",
      ["Turn off the tap while brushing your teeth.", "Buy bottled water for every meal.", "Rain falls often in the wet season.", "Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius."],
      "The paragraph lists ways to save water, so the missing sentence should be another water-saving tip."),
    S(2, 1, "Vocabulary in context", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nThe old bridge had become __hazardous__. Its railings were rusted, several planks were missing, and it shook whenever a tricycle crossed it. The town closed it until repairs could be made.\n\nAs used in the passage, \"hazardous\" most nearly means:",
      ["dangerous", "crowded", "beautiful", "expensive"],
      "Rusted railings, missing planks and shaking describe a dangerous bridge, which is why the town closed it."),
    S(2, 3, "Conclusion", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nIn a survey of 200 market vendors, 150 said they lost sales on rainy days because the market had no roof. After a roof was built over the main aisle, the same vendors reported that rainy-day sales were close to their usual level.\n\nWhich statement is best supported by the passage?",
      ["The roof helped vendors keep their sales on rainy days", "Most vendors left the market after the roof was built", "Rainy days happen less often since the roof was built", "Only half the vendors were asked about their sales"],
      "Sales on rainy days returned to near normal after the roof went up. The survey covered all 200 vendors, and the roof cannot change the weather."),

    # ---------- Drill only ----------
    S(0, 2, "Main idea", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nA good filing system saves time every day. When folders are labeled clearly and kept in order, any staff member can find a document in seconds. When they are not, people waste hours searching and important papers can be lost for good.\n\nWhat is the main idea?",
      ["An orderly filing system saves time and papers", "Folders should always be the same color", "Only one person should handle the files", "Papers are lost mainly because of floods"],
      "The first sentence states the point, and the rest contrasts order (quick finding) with disorder (lost time and papers)."),
    S(0, 3, "Inference", "Read the passage, then answer the question.\n\nThe notice at the pier said that all boats to the island were cancelled because of a storm signal. Ben read it, folded his ticket into his wallet and asked the guard where the nearest inn was.\n\nWhat can be inferred about Ben?",
      ["He expects to travel once the trips resume", "He plans to swim across to the island", "He has decided to sell his ticket", "He works as a guard at the pier"],
      "He keeps his ticket and looks for a place to stay, so he expects to sail when the trips resume."),
    S(0, 3, "Paragraph organization", "Arrange the sentences to form a logical paragraph.\n\n1. Because of this, farmers in the area now plant drought-tolerant rice.\n2. In recent years the dry season in the region has grown longer.\n3. They also store rainwater in small farm ponds.\n4. Many fields no longer get enough water for ordinary rice.",
      ["2, 4, 1, 3", "4, 2, 1, 3", "2, 1, 4, 3", "2, 4, 3, 1"],
      "Sentence 2 states the cause, 4 its effect on fields, 1 the farmers' response (\"Because of this\"), and 3 a second response (\"also\")."),
]
